 "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The spec is implemented, and `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_options.py` passes (676 passed). I read the diff and it matches the spec.\n\n- **`Option.get_error_hint`** in `src/click/core.py`: the hint is added only when `show_envvar` is set and `envvar` is truthy. It quotes each variable and joins them with `\", \"`. A comment explains the quotes: a name may contain a space or a comma.\n- **`Option.get_help_extra`** in `src/click/core.py`: an empty `envvar` now falls back to the auto-prefix name, the same as `None`. `extra[\"envvars\"]` is set only when `envvar` is truthy. The nested `if` is merged into one condition.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: two bullets under Unreleased, both ending with ``{pr}`3884` ``. One covers the sequence error message, the other the empty `envvar` help and error.\n\nI didn't touch `tests/test_options.py`, and I ran only the one command the spec lists, not the rest of the test suite.", "ttft_ms": 2227, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 6040, "uuid": "59f75baf-802a-4f9b-9480-f6d1b2b29358", "ttft_stream_ms": 1908, "time_to_request_ms": 17, "first_content_frame_ms": 1908, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
